			"Message": "feat(Project): Coordinate file dialog integration and Tauri event bridge across Land submodules\n\nSynchronize four Land submodules with complementary features:\n\n- Wind: Add ShowOpenDialog and ShowSaveDialog to FilesService with native file dialog integration via IPC to Mountain backend\n- Sky: Implement SkyBridge.ts - a new Tauri event bridge for sky:// channel communication, routing events to VS Code workbench APIs across 8 categories (Editor, Output, StatusBar, Progress, Terminal, Webview, Native, UI)\n- Grove: Fix string ownership in LanguageNamespace provider registration to eliminate lifetime issues\n- Mountain: Simplify entry point comments in Library.rs for clarity\n\nThis coordinated update completes the native file dialog integration in Wind's service layer while establishing the frontend IPC infrastructure in Sky for Mountain to drive UI updates via Tauri events.",
			"SHA": "cd535193ca7bddba82892fc8ff66dedbfc92b609"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-06T04:18:59Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Update Mountain submodule to 6e475d18\n\nAdvance the Mountain submodule pointer from 514c8544 to 6e475d18855d771efb72ca679e3efe481e15015e.\n\nThis routine coordination keeps the Land element dependencies synchronized.",
			"SHA": "f881cb77f481d46cc4b7d7569d42517567a54676"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-06T04:14:13Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Implement real document loading and message dialog selection\n\nEnhance Window service message dialogs (showInformationMessage, showWarningMessage, showErrorMessage) to properly handle the items parameter by sending gRPC requests with items to Mountain and returning the selected item from the response.\n\nEnhance Workspace service openTextDocument to fetch actual file content from Mountain via fs.readFile instead of returning mock data. Implement full TextDocument interface with proper getText(range), lineAt, offsetAt, positionAt, validateRange, validatePosition methods. Add language detection based on file extension mapping.\n\nAlso add workspace folder DTO conversion to VSCode.WorkspaceFolder objects in AcceptWorkspaceData handler. Remove stale TODO comments about event stream emitters and WorkspaceConfiguration that have been addressed.\n\nThese changes complete the basic document opening flow, enabling real file content to be displayed in the editor with proper language detection.",
			"SHA": "02335a6eb51aacbb6b4cab5e8aec3f60ace7377b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-06T04:13:21Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Project): Coordinate Cocoon webview IPC and Maintain gitmodules fixes\n\nUpdate two Land submodules with complementary improvements:\n\nCocoon: Implement actual gRPC notifications in WindowService's IPC proxy\nto complete the webview lifecycle integration with Mountain backend. SendNotification\nnow posts messages via webview.postMessage, SendRequest returns undefined as\nfire-and-forget, and dispose callback notifies Mountain to destroy the webview\npanel via webview.dispose.\n\nMaintain: Fix .gitmodules formatting by removing incorrect indentation from the\nDocumentation/Rust submodule entry and add ignore=all directive to prevent local\nsubmodule modifications from cluttering git status.\n\nThis coordinated update completes the webview lifecycle IPC while keeping the\nMaintain workspace clean.",
			"SHA": "664d25f1c09f11757bfc579195ac020d189b6ec2"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-06T04:07:13Z",
			"File": [
				"⡿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				5
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Coordinate POSIX shell compliance across Land submodules\n\nUpdate five submodules to use POSIX-compliant sh shebang instead of bash in build scripts:\n- Output: Make shell scripts POSIX-compliant (prepublishOnly.sh, Run.sh)\n- Rest: Convert bash-specific scripts to portable POSIX sh syntax\n- Wind: Use POSIX sh shebang for build scripts\n- Worker: Use POSIX-compliant sh shebang in build scripts\n- Cocoon: Implement progress IPC notifications to Mountain\n\nThe Cocoon submodule also includes a new feature: implementing actual gRPC notifications for the WithProgress API, enabling Mountain backend to display real-time progress indicators during extension execution.\n\nThis coordinated update ensures consistent shell compatibility across the Land ecosystem while adding the progress notification capability to the extension host.",
			"SHA": "dc77d54e7ce0cd5d655a5a489364e659958226de"
		}
	],
